    "teach_7": {
      "id": "teach_7",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Percent relations between digits are just fraction relations.\n\nIf the units digit is 75% of the tens digit, then u=3t/4.\n\nThat means t must be a multiple of 4 for u to be an integer digit.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_7_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_7_step": {
      "id": "teach_7_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Suppose t is one more than h and h+t=15.\nThen h=7, t=8.\nUnits = 75% of 8 = 6.\nNumber = 786.\n\nDigit restrictions help us reject impossible values early.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_7"
        }
      ]
    },
